# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*
# ...except the documented template, which holds names and comments only and
# must never hold a value.
!.env.example

# Claude Code MCP server config. Local-only because the useful form of it is
# per-developer: the URL carries `project_ref`, which pins WHICH Supabase
# project your MCP session talks to. Committed, that silently makes production
# the default target for everyone who opens the repo. Copy the template and set
# your own ref (a preview branch, a personal project, or production if you mean
# it). Note git does NOT stop tracking a file just because it is listed here —
# this only works because `.mcp.json` was untracked with `git rm --cached`.
.mcp.json
# ...except the documented template, which holds a placeholder ref only and
# must never hold a real project reference.
!.mcp.json.example

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# claude
claude.md
.claude/docs/business-settings-plan.md
.claude/OFFERINGS_MODEL.md
.claude/EXPLORE_BUSINESS_INFO.md
.claude/LANDING_REDESIGN.md
.claude/BRAND_ROLLOUT.md
.claude/EXPLORE_PUBLIC_NAV.md
.claude/USER_STORIES.md
.claude/APP_REVAMP.md
.claude/CATALOGUES.md
.claude/EVENTS.md
.claude/EVENTS_TABLE.md
.claude/ERROR_HANDLING.md
.claude/SHOP_GALLERY.md

# Live git worktrees of this same repo. Each is a full second checkout with its
# own node_modules, so `git add -A` in the parent would stage two entire copies
# of the tree. Git never tracks them anyway — this only stops the accident.
.claude/worktrees/

# Runtime verification log appended by supabase/scripts/pull-live.sh. The SQL
# probes in this dir ARE checked in; this generated log is not.
supabase/reports/pull-live.log

# Variable font cuts: the image renderer (Satori) cannot parse them, so they
# are never the file to commit. Static cuts only.
assets/fonts/*-Variable.ttf
.claude/SENTRY_TRIAGE.md
